<article class="env-lemma" id="00X5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00X5">Lemma <span data-tag="00X5">7.14.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{D}$ be sites. Let $u : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$ be continuous. Assume all the categories $(\mathcal{I}_ V^ u)^{opp}$ of Section <a href="/tag/00VC" data-tag="00VC">7.5</a> are filtered. Then $u$ defines a morphism of sites $\mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}$, in other words $u_ s$ is exact. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $u_ s$ is the left adjoint of $u^ s$ we see that $u_ s$ is right exact, see Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0039" data-tag="0039">4.24.6</a>. Hence it suffices to show that $u_ s$ is left exact. In other words we have to show that $u_ s$ commutes with finite limits. Because the categories $\mathcal{I}_ Y^{opp}$ are filtered we see that $u_ p$ commutes with finite limits, see Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/002W" data-tag="002W">4.19.2</a> (this also uses the description of limits in $\textit{PSh}$, see Section <a href="/tag/00VB" data-tag="00VB">7.4</a>). And since sheafification commutes with finite limits as well (Lemma <a href="/tag/00WJ" data-tag="00WJ">7.10.15</a>) we conclude because $u_ s = \#  \circ u_ p$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>